    {
      "@id": "skills/tools/folio-core/deployment-auth.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "The API decides with ODRL (issues #1180, #1207)",
      "prov:value": "**Half built, 2026-09-23 (#1207).** The API server no longer compares a\nviewer < collaborator < owner ladder. `src/core/rbac.ts` treats the gateway's\ntier as a declared actor (`viewer`, `collaborator`, `owner` in\n`cat-harness/scenarios/actors/`), each route names the ODRL **action** it performs,\nand `policies/http-gateway.jsonld` says which tier holds which action. It\nreproduces what the ladder allowed. An explicit `X-User-Actor` header, once the\ngateway sends one, takes precedence over the tier. What is still to build is\nsteps 1 and 4 below: the gateway mapping a login to a finer-grained actor, and\na relationship engine. The same policies govern BPMN task execution\n([`task-authorization`](../../process/process-core/task-authorization.md)).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1207",
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
